  "description": "AGSC-07-12: the compatibility pin of the seven Harness file kinds. For every valid composition case of the set — the selections of `compose-0011`, `-0012`, `-0013`, `-0015`, `-0017`, `-0018`, `-0019` and `-0020`, whose items and selections are repeated here so that this case stands alone, and one more, `all-seven-kinds`, that fills the per-Concept and per-Procedure kinds — the case carries the SHA-256 of every file the Harness writes, keyed by its path relative to `dist/harness/<name>/`, for a build instant, a content version, a site base and a licence fixed in `fixed`; `spec_version` is fixed too, because the provenance header of every file states the version of the specification the tool implements, which a pin must not depend on. The values were produced by the 1.0.1 engine and are a pin, not a new behaviour: a later MINOR may add files beside the Harness directory (AGSC-07-25, AGSC-07-29, AGSC-07-30) and must not move a byte of these. `compose-0021`, `-0022`, `-0023`, `-0001` and `-0002` are not in the set because their compositions are invalid and emit no Harness (AGSC-07-17). The case does not claim cross-implementation byte-identity of the Harness, which AGSC-04-24 withholds until the `harness/` area has cases; it holds the reference engine to its own bytes across versions.",
